From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 16:56:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm: pass the virtio-pci INTX line count to the GPEX

0115 publishes the virtio-pci layout to the xenpvh machine by reading the seven
xenstore keys libxl writes, and 0215 teaches xen-pvh-common to hand out one INTX
line per PCI slot when cfg.pci_intx_irq_count says so. Nothing connects the two:
0115 reads irq_first and stops, so the count stays at the GPEX default of four
however many lines libxl put in the guest device tree.

That mismatch is silent and it is not cosmetic. libxl's interrupt-map wraps as

    irq = irq_first + ((pin + slot) % num_irqs)

so a guest DT written for sixteen lines against a GPEX wired for four pairs
slots onto shared level-triggered SPIs. virtio-blk and virtio-net recover on the
next kick; virtio-snd's used-buffer interrupt and a decode session's DQBUF
completion are their only wake-up sources, so they stall with nothing to recover
them. libxl has published num_irqs alongside irq_first since the virtio-pci host
was introduced (tools/libs/light/libxl_dm.c), so the value is already there.

Read it, and read it on its own `ok`: a DomD paired with an older libxl would
have the other seven keys and not this one, and failing the whole layout over it
would take PCI away from a guest that works today. Absent or zero keeps the GPEX
default, which is what xen-pvh-common does with pci_intx_irq_count == 0.

Depends-on: 0115-hw-arm-accept-xenpv-as-an-alias-for-the-xenpvh-machi.patch
Depends-on: 0215-v10-xen-pvh-common-one-INTX-line-per-virtio-pci-slot.patch
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream fork / xenstore layout is fork-only]
---
diff --git a/hw/arm/xen-pvh.c b/hw/arm/xen-pvh.c
index 6a66478af0c..c77c6fa6775 100644
--- a/hw/arm/xen-pvh.c
+++ b/hw/arm/xen-pvh.c
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@ static void xen_arm_pci_layout_from_xenstore(XenPVHMachineState *s)
     struct qemu_xs_handle *h;
     bool ok = true;
     uint64_t ecam_base, ecam_size, mem_base, mem_size;
-    uint64_t pref_base, pref_size, irq_first;
+    uint64_t pref_base, pref_size, irq_first, num_irqs;
 
     if (s->cfg.pci_ecam.size) {
         return;         /* explicitly configured; nothing to do */
@@ -119,6 +119,21 @@ static void xen_arm_pci_layout_from_xenstore(XenPVHMachineState *s)
     pref_base = xen_arm_xs_read_u64(h, "prefetch_mem_base", &ok);
     pref_size = xen_arm_xs_read_u64(h, "prefetch_mem_size", &ok);
     irq_first = xen_arm_xs_read_u64(h, "irq_first", &ok);
+    /*
+     * num_irqs is read on its own `ok`: libxl has published it since the
+     * virtio-pci host was introduced, but a DomD paired with an older libxl
+     * would have the other seven keys and not this one, and failing the whole
+     * layout over it would take PCI away from a guest that works without it.
+     * Absent or zero means "the GPEX default", which is what xen-pvh-common
+     * does with pci_intx_irq_count == 0.
+     */
+    {
+        bool have_num_irqs = true;
+        num_irqs = xen_arm_xs_read_u64(h, "num_irqs", &have_num_irqs);
+        if (!have_num_irqs) {
+            num_irqs = 0;
+        }
+    }
     qemu_xen_xs_close(h);
 
     if (!ok || !ecam_size) {
@@ -129,6 +144,14 @@ static void xen_arm_pci_layout_from_xenstore(XenPVHMachineState *s)
     s->cfg.pci_mmio      = (MemMapEntry) { mem_base, mem_size };
     s->cfg.pci_mmio_high = (MemMapEntry) { pref_base, pref_size };
     s->cfg.pci_intx_irq_base = irq_first;
+    /*
+     * One INTX line per PCI slot instead of the four INTA-D lines. libxl's
+     * interrupt-map wraps as irq = irq_first + ((pin + slot) % num_irqs), so
+     * the guest DT and the GPEX have to agree on num_irqs or two slots share a
+     * level-triggered SPI -- fatal for virtio-snd and for a decode session,
+     * whose completion interrupt is their only wake-up source.
+     */
+    s->cfg.pci_intx_irq_count = num_irqs;
 }
 
 static void (*xen_pvh_common_machine_init)(MachineState *ms);
